			<aux name="Fossil Fuel Extraction\nProductivity" access="input">
				<dimensions>
					<dim name="Run"/>
				</dimensions>
				<eqn>{Enter equation for use when not hooked up to other models}</eqn>
				<units>GtC/c$/Years</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="C per N in fertillizer">
				<doc>${External Parameter}
The parameter represents corresponds to a physical constant derived from the chemical equation of the fertilizer production process.

The parameter value was derived with technical support from Magdalena Blanz.

</doc>
				<eqn>0.321</eqn>
				<units>tC/tN</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Energy factor">
				<doc>${External Parameter}
The parameter represents the additional energy required in fertilizer production beyond the carbon used as feedstock. In conventional ammonia production via steam methane reforming (SMR), roughly two-thirds of natural gas is used as feedstock and one-third is combusted to supply process heat, implying total natural gas input of about 1.5× the feedstock requirement. 
This relationship is consistent with estimates reported in the literature on ammonia production technologies. 
References: 
Karibe, H., Sair, S., Faik, A., &amp; Ait Ousaleh, H. (2025). Electrified steam methane reforming: A review of heating technologies, challenges, and prospects. International Journal of Hydrogen Energy, 133, 200–213. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2025.04.475
Rouwenhorst, K. H. R., Krzywda, P. M., Benes, N. E., Mul, G., &amp; Lefferts, L. (2021). Ammonia production technologies. In A. Valera-Medina &amp; R. Banares-Alcantara (Eds.), Techno-economic challenges of green ammonia as an energy vector (pp. 41–83). Elsevier. https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-12-820560-0.00004-7
Synthesis Gas reformers https://www.owlnet.rice.edu/~ceng403/nh3ref97.html
</doc>
				<eqn>1.5</eqn>
				<units>Dimensionless</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Price of fertilizer feedstock">
				<dimensions>
					<dim name="Run"/>
				</dimensions>
				<eqn>UNIT_GtC_per_MtN_in_fertilizer*Energy_factor/Fossil_Fuel_Extraction_Productivity</eqn>
				<units>c$*Year/(Million*tN)</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="UNIT tC per GtC">
				<doc>${Unit}
</doc>
				<eqn>1000000000</eqn>
				<units>tC/GtC</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="UNIT tN per MtN">
				<doc>${Unit}
</doc>
				<eqn>1000000</eqn>
				<units>tN/MtN</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="UNIT GtC per MtN in fertilizer">
				<dimensions>
					<dim name="Run"/>
				</dimensions>
				<eqn>(C_per_N_in_fertillizer/UNIT_tC_per_GtC)*UNIT_tN_per_MtN</eqn>
				<units>GtC/MtN</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Amount of natural gas needed for fertilizer">
				<dimensions>
					<dim name="Run"/>
				</dimensions>
				<eqn>Energy_factor*total_yearly_consumption*C_per_N_in_fertillizer/UNIT_MtC_to_GtC</eqn>
				<units>GtC/Year</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Fossil Fuel Extraction Carbon" access="input">
				<dimensions>
					<dim name="Run"/>
				</dimensions>
				<eqn>{Enter equation for use when not hooked up to other models}</eqn>
				<units>gtC/Year</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="UNIT MtC to GtC">
				<doc>${Unit}
</doc>
				<dimensions>
					<dim name="Run"/>
				</dimensions>
				<eqn>1000</eqn>
				<units>(Million*tC)/GtC</units>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Ratio of natural gas needed for fertilizer over natural gas production">
				<dimensions>
					<dim name="Run"/>
